Tezbar standalone color-picker Rust extension

Extracted and adapted from Tezbar, baseline fe71ca87f21ac4ff31505010c228f8abda0f2a89.
App-derived Rust and helper source is Apache-2.0: see LICENSE.
Behavior and original artwork derive from the installed Raycast extension.
Raycast extension source is MIT: see licenses/raycast-extensions-MIT.txt.
Original author and source provenance: SOURCE.json and extension.json.
Installed bundle revision is unknown; current upstream metadata in provenance
must not be represented as the installed revision.

Color naming tables: color-namer 1.4.0, Copyright (c) Zeke Sikelianos 2016,
MIT (licenses/color-namer-MIT.md). NTC names: Chirag Mehta, CC BY 2.5,
https://chir.ag/projects/name-that-color/ and
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/ .
Original NTC notice/source and legal code: licenses/ntc/.
The tables were converted from JavaScript into JSON and hexadecimal colors
normalized; the Rust port retains these converted tables. Attribution and the
CC BY 2.5 license apply to the NTC data; this package is not MIT-only.
The tray PNG reproduces the baseline adapter's locally drawn eyedropper mask.
Original installed icon and color wheel PNG are retained without a new ownership
or trademark claim.

The packaged Windows sampler is an app-derived source adaptation, not a
byte-identical copy: it adds terminating errors, headless -Check and the shared
windows-modules.ps1 bootstrap. That Apache-2.0 bootstrap imports only required
OS PowerShell modules from PSHOME; OS module binaries are not redistributed.
The sampler UI/capture implementation is retained. See SOURCE.json for input
provenance and hashes of these packaged derivative sources.
